The clang-format wheels on PyPI are built by
https://github.com/ssciwr/clang-format-wheel from the llvm-project source
release of the same version, with LLVM and Clang linked statically into the
clang-format binary. The wheels include only the wheel project's own
Apache-2.0 license, so this directory adds the license files of the code
that is compiled into the binary:

  llvm/LICENSE.TXT    llvm/LICENSE.TXT of llvm-project
  clang/LICENSE.TXT   clang/LICENSE.TXT of llvm-project
  llvm/NOTICES        notices of the files in LLVM's Support library that
                      come from other projects

They were checked against LLVM 23, at the llvmorg-23.1.3 tag of
https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project.

The musllinux wheels, which the Alpine images install, also contain
libstdc++ and libgcc_s in clang_format.libs. auditwheel copied them from
the Alpine gcc package of the image the wheels were built in. They are
licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception, and
gcc/ holds GCC's COPYING3 and COPYING.RUNTIME from the releases/gcc-14.2.0
tag of https://gcc.gnu.org/git/gcc.git. The image has gcc/ only when the
installed wheel contains these libraries.

auditwheel names the Alpine packages in
clang_format-<version>.dist-info/sboms/auditwheel.cdx.json, which pip
installs into the virtual environment. The build accepts a wheel only when
they are the GCC build that gcc/ was checked against, libstdc++ and libgcc
14.2.0-r6 from Alpine 3.22. The APKINDEX of Alpine 3.22 main names aports
commit fbf60319be3bbaf6dd32ef55cc6fb7189e05c266 as their source. At that
commit, the build recipe main/gcc applies its patches to the GCC 14.2.0
release, whose SHA-512 it lists. These two archives are the corresponding
source of the libraries. They are attached to the GitHub release of each
version of the image, which the last line of the image's source file links
to, and the GCC archive has its upstream signature next to it.

